  "repo_truth": "The parent submits an immutable 59-path HCM-2.3 implementation subject after remediating every Review 5 finding and completing the engine, CLI, workspace, HCM-2.2, cross-platform, validation, packaging, preservation, and GitNexus proof walls. The dispatch excludes itself and asserts no CLEAN conclusion, commit, closeout, or broader authority.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Remain read-only; replay all 59 hashes, ordering, aggregate fingerprint, dispatch self-exclusion, branch codex/hcm-2-3-planning, HEAD 3c49fa2c6d653f4b1a703d1d5c5196147b003533, and selected-handoff authority before review.",
    "Review every production, test, fixture, contract, proof, and prior-dispatch entry against complete HCM-2.3 authority, including correctness, security, recovery, retained-handle native filesystem safety, strict fresh/recovery separation, reverse reachability, shared byte bounds, engine-owned release identity, schema source-kind containment, concurrency, exact inventories, CLI behavior, and HCM-2.2 preservation.",
    "Return findings first, ordered Critical, Required, Optional, Nit, with exact file/line evidence, violated invariant, failure mode, smallest bounded repair, and missing verification."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "No edits, staging, commits, handoff/ledger writes, branch changes, preservation/archive access, or user task hops.",
    "No HCM-2.4, Phase 3+, Phase 4 SDK/transport, Cargo/package/dependency changes, resolver redesign, built-in namespace expansion, repository authority widening, or HCM-2.2 reinterpretation.",
    "Do not accept tests or proof prose as a success conclusion; verify implementation and regressions independently."
  ],
  "tasks": [
    "Invoke the required skills, read repository AGENTS.md and this complete dispatch, and return BLOCKED on any manifest, branch, HEAD, handoff, dispatch-exclusion, or authority mismatch.",
    "Review tests first and map every mandatory HCM-2.3 behavior and explicit schema-root authorization to an effective regression.",
    "Re-audit all Review 5 findings: final post-hook canonical fingerprint/native-version revalidation on fresh and recovery paths; pre-mutation reverse reachability and direct committed-chain replay/expiry proof; and strict fresh CreateNew absence/exclusive creation versus exact established-intent recovery.",
    "Test adversarial changed/deleted/same-byte-restored-mtime canonical publication, orphan tombstone/ledger/result/artifact controls, malformed valid-name records, duplicate citations, equal/unequal closure and semantic residue, and zero-delta refusal.",
    "Re-audit Review 4 retained-handle/path identity, scratch source separation, engine-owned consumer version, and shared exact 1 MiB document bounds.",
    "Audit BuiltIn fixed definitions/schemas containment and allowlist-only bytes; Repository request-root-only containment; cache/error precedence; the sole HCM-2.3 request root; and the unchanged high-level schema resolver.",
    "Audit recovery-first authority, complete request/plan revalidation, native identity/version binding, symlink/hard-link/non-regular/mutation/traversal refusal, exact inventory bounds, crash prefixes, idempotency, races, durability, and zero-mutation refusal.",
    "Audit generic registration, selection closure, operation context, canonical YAML, intake evaluation, lineage persistence, refusal tuples, ledger/tombstone closure, and every direct read/replay path.",
    "Audit the actual CLI boundary for ten fixed commands, explicit authority, stable exits, shared bounded input, human/JSON rendering, cwd/path/stdin handling, fresh-process recovery, and no per-kind dispatch.",
    "Verify control-pack status is no broader than executable evidence and no forbidden path or authority entered the subject.",
    "Return CLEAN only with zero Critical, Required, Optional, and Nit findings; otherwise return CHANGES_REQUIRED or BLOCKED and do not repair files."
  ],
